  "files": [
    {
      "section": "Clinical Analysis",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 25 trust",
      "description": "Imaging tests for this Operator showed blurry outlines of internal organs with visible dark spots. Unusually high concentrations of Originium particles were present in her circulatory system, indicating infection and confirming her as Infected at this stage. \n\n[Cell-Originium Assimilation] 5% \nCurrently no visible symptoms. \n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.24u/L \nMinor stage of infection, currently no discernible physical effects."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 1",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 50 trust",
      "description": "Meteor is an easy-going forest warden. \nTime was, she and her fellow wardens protected the endless forests of Kazimierz, until she contracted Oripathy and was forced into exile. She joined Rhodes Island after several stops in between. \nKind and caring, Meteor loves big get-togethers and often takes the lead herself. Despite her age, she is very reliable."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 2",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 100 trust",
      "description": "Meteor doesn't care much for electronic devices. \nTrying to get some gizmo to work is worse than having Oripathy to her. Naturally, coming to our island was quite a culture shock for her; more than most any other new operator. \nEven after all this time, she still avoids electronics."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 3",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 150 trust",
      "description": "As composite bows replace the traditional kind, Meteor bucks the trend by sticking to the old ways. \nIt is to her a commemoration of her past, the other forest wardens who fought with her, and her life in the woods. \nGiven her skill, she easily meets expected damage output metrics without the advantages provided by a composite bow."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 4",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 200 trust",
      "description": "After leaving the forest, Meteor wandered for a long time. She went endured the hardships of the modern world and saw how much the people feared Oripathy. \nNone of that made her lose faith, though. She finally found Rhodes Island and requested to serve as an operator while undergoing treatment. The island couldn't turn away a talent like her."
    }
  ]
}
